00:39:20,141 --> 00:39:27,100
snap the landing gear to stop the plane, then there's a really good reason to have it.

452
00:39:27,101 --> 00:39:33,240
Every year the concrete industry holds a massive convention to show off what's new in the business.

453
00:39:33,241 --> 00:39:37,140
It's called the world of concrete.

454
00:39:37,141 --> 00:39:39,361
The world of concrete is a blast.

455
00:39:39,362 --> 00:39:44,140
The world of concrete is so full of people with new ideas, fresh ideas.

456
00:39:44,141 --> 00:39:50,140
They're working together, they're coming up with new mixed designs, they're making new things possible we've never seen before.

457
00:39:52,140 --> 00:39:58,140
It's a giant concrete candy store where the latest tools of the trade are on display.

458
00:39:58,141 --> 00:40:05,840
At center stage, a new generation of mixing trucks that help supply a steady stream of

459
00:40:05,841 --> 00:40:08,780
concrete at the construction site.

460
00:40:08,781 --> 00:40:13,240
These state of the art mixers use heavy duty pumping systems to push the concrete where

461
00:40:13,241 --> 00:40:14,240
it's needed.

462
00:40:14,241 --> 00:40:22,560
You have to have a mixture that flows through the pipes from the pump at the base of the

463
00:40:22,561 --> 00:40:23,560
structure.

464
00:40:23,561 --> 00:40:28,320
And you want to make sure that the concrete doesn't set before it gets all the way up to the top.

465
00:40:29,100 --> 00:40:32,260
There's much that's hot and new and exciting in concrete today.

466
00:40:32,261 --> 00:40:38,420
The things that strike my fancy the most with concrete is the creative use of color and finish.

467
00:40:40,200 --> 00:40:48,400
Modern concrete home builders are taking advantage of techniques and ideas that were pioneered by legendary American architect Frank Lloyd Wright.

468
00:40:48,401 --> 00:40:55,400
He just used concrete in ways that other people hadn't used it before.

469
00:40:55,401 --> 00:40:59,400
Wright was once referred to as a rebel in concrete.

470
00:40:59,401 --> 00:41:05,400
He believed that a building should develop out of and exist with its natural surroundings.

471
00:41:05,401 --> 00:41:09,400
Wright personally showcased that philosophy in the late 30s

472
00:41:09,401 --> 00:41:16,400
with his legendary design and construction of the so-called Falling Water Concrete House in Pennsylvania.

473
00:41:16,401 --> 00:41:21,100
Frank Lloyd Wright used concrete as art, really.

474
00:41:21,101 --> 00:41:22,400
He liked to expose concrete.

475
00:41:22,401 --> 00:41:26,400
He used molds to develop patterns on his structures.

476
00:41:26,401 --> 00:41:32,400
But the futuristic Johnson Wax Building might be Wright's greatest work.

477
00:41:32,401 --> 00:41:39,100
Built in Racine, Wisconsin in 1936, it used the weight-bearing capabilities of concrete

478
00:41:39,101 --> 00:41:43,400
to create a futuristic working environment in a corporate headquarters.

479
00:41:43,401 --> 00:41:51,460
White's early use of concrete blocks has led the way for dramatic new uses of concrete

480
00:41:51,461 --> 00:41:54,180
in modern home building.

481
00:41:54,181 --> 00:42:00,280
These insulating concrete forms are gaining widespread acceptance.

482
00:42:00,281 --> 00:42:05,920
I would say the use of concrete for home building is probably the single most revolutionary

483
00:42:05,921 --> 00:42:06,920
use of concrete.

484
00:42:06,921 --> 00:42:11,400
Polystyrene forms that are stacked in place with polystyrene on both sides.

485
00:42:11,401 --> 00:42:15,240
Once you form the shape of your structure or home, then you place concrete inside.

486
00:42:15,820 --> 00:42:21,420
So once the concrete hardens, you have a super strong home that's also very energy efficient because of the insulation.

487
00:42:21,580 --> 00:42:23,280
It's also very quiet because of the concrete.

488
00:42:23,920 --> 00:42:30,600
We can add any kind of external finishing from siding, brick, stucco.

489
00:42:30,840 --> 00:42:32,860
So they look just like any other house on the block.

490
00:42:32,940 --> 00:42:35,500
They don't look like a big gray concrete square.

491
00:42:35,501 --> 00:42:38,760
They can look like any home you see in a typical American neighborhood.

492
00:42:38,761 --> 00:42:45,200
Concrete's lasting legacy will be its widespread use.

493
00:42:45,201 --> 00:42:49,120
The same substance that makes it possible to build something as simple and benign as

494
00:42:49,121 --> 00:42:57,000
a driveway also makes it possible to construct a military missile silo.

495
00:42:57,001 --> 00:43:01,640
Concrete is an essential part of civic icons around the world, from the Gateway Arch in

496
00:43:01,641 --> 00:43:08,520
St. Louis to the Space Needle in Seattle and the Opera House in Sydney, Australia.

497
00:43:08,521 --> 00:43:13,840
When concrete was fashioned into the Berlin Wall, it separated an entire country.

498
00:43:13,841 --> 00:43:19,500
But when it was used in the English Channel Tunnel, it brought two nations together.

499
00:43:19,501 --> 00:43:25,800
And when it was poured into the gigantic foundation of the Patronus Towers in Kuala Lumpur, it

500
00:43:25,801 --> 00:43:30,800
anchored the tallest structure in the world again.

501
00:43:30,801 --> 00:43:35,180
Every day a new concrete building makes a new statement somewhere.

502
00:43:35,181 --> 00:43:37,760
For the future, the sky's the limit.

503
00:43:38,860 --> 00:43:40,680
You could make concrete on the moon.

504
00:43:40,880 --> 00:43:43,480
There's no reason you couldn't make Portland cement on the moon

505
00:43:43,481 --> 00:43:45,880
because the raw materials already exist there.

506
00:43:46,140 --> 00:43:51,160
People have looked at the moon rocks and realized that what they call lunar concrete is entirely possible.

507
00:43:51,660 --> 00:43:56,980
The composition of the moon, of a lunar rock, is not that different from that of Portland cement.

508
00:43:57,580 --> 00:43:58,840
All you have to do is figure out how to make water.

509
00:43:58,841 --> 00:44:05,840
Perhaps with space stations ultimately we may be able to take materials into space,

510
00:44:05,841 --> 00:44:11,840
mix it and make concrete as we know it here on Earth and use it for construction purposes.

511
00:44:11,841 --> 00:44:17,840
I think sky's the limit. There's no place that you can't go and see concrete

